Feature: Channel-wise Sales Performance Analysis for Biosimilar Brands

  This feature analyzes the sales performance of biosimilar brands (kanjinti, mvasi, riabni) across different sales channels (e.g., online, retail, mobile) by aggregating sales metrics from the table purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack. The analysis filters data within 36 months from a specified cdl_effective_date and groups results by brand, product, market, competitor flag, and channel.

  Background:
    Given the source table is "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack"
    And the columns used are:
      | brand_normalized_name      | string  |
      | normalized_name            | string  |
      | market_normalized_name     | string  |
      | competitor_flag            | boolean |
      | channel_name               | string  |
      | transaction_timestamp      | timestamp|
      | integrated_units           | bigint  |
      | integrated_normalized_units| bigint  |
      | integrated_dollars         | bigint  |
      | cdl_effective_date         | string  |
    And the brands to include are "kanjinti", "mvasi", and "riabni"
    And the sales data must be within 36 months from the provided reference cdl_effective_date parameter "<reference_cdl_effective_date>" in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And the grouping attributes are brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    And the aggregation metrics are sum of integrated_units, sum of integrated_normalized_units, sum of integrated_dollars

  Scenario Outline: Happy Path - Aggregate sales for valid biosimilar brands and valid cdl_effective_date within 36 months
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name in <brand_list>
    And each record has a non-null, valid cdl_effective_date in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And the difference in months between <reference_cdl_effective_date> and cdl_effective_date is less than or equal to 36
    When the data is filtered for brand_normalized_name in <brand_list>
    And the data is filtered for cdl_effective_date within 36 months from <reference_cdl_effective_date>
    Then the result should group records by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    And the result should show sum of integrated_units, sum of integrated_normalized_units, sum of integrated_dollars for each group
    And the output should include all unique channel_name values present in the filtered data

    Examples:
      | brand_list                      | reference_cdl_effective_date |
      | ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"] | 2023-01-01                  |
      | ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"] | 2022-06-15                  |

  Scenario: Error - Record with null cdl_effective_date
    Given a record has brand_normalized_name in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    And cdl_effective_date is null
    When the data is filtered for cdl_effective_date within 36 months from <reference_cdl_effective_date>
    Then the record should be excluded from the result set

  Scenario: Error - Record with invalid cdl_effective_date format
    Given a record has brand_normalized_name in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    And cdl_effective_date is not in "yyyy-MM-dd" format (e.g., "2023/01/01", "01-01-2023", "invalid-date")
    When the data is filtered for cdl_effective_date within 36 months from <reference_cdl_effective_date>
    Then the record should be excluded from the result set

  Scenario: Error - Record with brand not in the specified list
    Given a record has brand_normalized_name not in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    When the data is filtered for brand_normalized_name in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    Then the record should be excluded from the result set

  Scenario Outline: Error - Record outside 36 month window
    Given a record has brand_normalized_name in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    And cdl_effective_date is in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And the difference in months between <reference_cdl_effective_date> and cdl_effective_date is greater than 36
    When the data is filtered for cdl_effective_date within 36 months from <reference_cdl_effective_date>
    Then the record should be excluded from the result set

    Examples:
      | reference_cdl_effective_date | cdl_effective_date |
      | 2023-01-01                  | 2019-12-31         |
      | 2022-06-15                  | 2018-05-01         |

  Scenario: Output - Channel-wise aggregation includes all present channels
    Given the filtered data contains channel_name values "online", "retail", "mobile", "other"
    When the data is grouped by channel_name
    Then the output should include a row for each channel_name present in the filtered data

  Scenario: Output - Aggregation with zero sales
    Given a group has no records after filtering
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then the output should not include a row for that group

  Scenario: Output - Data type and format validation
    Given the output is generated
    Then brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, channel_name are strings
    And competitor_flag is boolean
    And sum of integrated_units, sum of integrated_normalized_units, sum of integrated_dollars are integers

  Scenario: Error - No valid records after filtering
    Given all records are excluded due to invalid brand, invalid cdl_effective_date, or outside 36 month window
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then the output should be an empty result set

  Scenario: Error - Handling of duplicate records
    Given duplicate records exist for the same group (same values for all grouping columns)
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then the sum of integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars should include all duplicates

  Scenario: Error - Handling of null sales metrics
    Given a record has null values for integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, or integrated_dollars
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then null values should be treated as zero in the sum

  Scenario: Output - Sorting of results
    Given the output is generated
    When the results are returned
    Then the output should be sorted by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name in ascending order

  Scenario: Output - Output format
    Given the output is generated
    Then the output should be a table with columns:
      | brand_normalized_name      |
      | normalized_name            |
      | market_normalized_name     |
      | competitor_flag            |
      | channel_name               |
      | sum_integrated_units       |
      | sum_integrated_normalized_units |
      | sum_integrated_dollars     |
